{title: King of Kings}
{subtitle: König aller Könige}
{song_number: 143}
{language: en}
{tempo: 68}
{key: D}

{start_of_verse: 1}
In the [D]darkness we were [G]waiting, without hope, [A]without light,
till from [D]Heaven You came [G]running. There was mer[A]cy in Your eyes.
To ful[D]fil the law and [G]prophets, to a vir[A]gin came the Word
from a [D]throne of endless [G]glory to a cra[A]dle in the [D]dirt.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
To re[D]veal the kingdom [G]coming and to re[A]concile the lost,
to re[D]deem the whole cre[G]ation You did not [A]despise the cross.
For e[D]ven in Your [G]suffering, You saw to [A]the other side,
knowing this [D]was our sal[G]vation, Jesus, for [A]our sake You [D]died.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[D]Praise the Father, [G]praise the Son, [Bm]praise the Spirit, [Asus4]three [A]in one.
[D]God of Glory, [G]majesty, [Bm]praise for[G]ever [A]to the King of [D]Kings.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 3}
And the [D]morning that You [G]rose, all of heav[A]en held its breath
till that [D]stone was moved for [G]good, for the Lamb [A]had conquered death.
And the [D]dead rose from their [G]tombs, and the an[A]gels stood in awe,
for the [D]souls of all who'd [G]come to the Fa[A]ther are re[D]stored.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
And the [D]Church of Christ was [G]born, then the Spir[A]it lit the flame.
Now this [D]Gospel truth of [G]old shall not kneel, [A]shall not faint.
By His [D]blood and in His [G]Name, in His free[A]dom I am free,
for the [D]love of Jesus [G]Christ who has res[A]urrected [D]me.
{end_of_verse}
